  "notes": "Registry note: struggling to drink water from the glass tube after tethering. Mean water intake 2.98 mL/day over 10 days, the lowest in the batch, consistent with that note. verdict_2026_08_19: SCOREABLE on the 39.7 h run. Hypnogram WAKE 43.3% / NREM 52.1%, r@1min 0.495 (bar 0.30). verdict_2026_08_27 (full 20.1 h): EEG FLOATING ALL RUN, 0.3% usable, 55 uV, slope -0.10, lf/hf 1.25 under a floor p99 of 5.06. Its chip's ground was weak for the entire run (~1300 uV against 4314 uV the day before) and never recovered on its own, which rules out settling after handling. \u2705 EMG IS REAL, not a floating input: 98.4% usable at 30 uV with a dark/light amplitude ratio of 2.73x, which is genuine state dependence. The fault was on the EEG side of the tether chain, not the implant. \u2b50 Was SCOREABLE before CSD (39.7 h run, hypnogram r@1min 0.495) and gives no EEG here, so it drops out of the paired recovery comparison. verdict_2026_08_28 (80 s check): \u2705 BACK. Chip floor 1347 -> 5026 uV, EEG 91 uV, slope -1.43, lf/hf 13.75 against a floor p99 of 1.88. Recoverable, and recovered 20 h too late.\n",
